{
  "_note": "Uniswap v3 swap-path allowlist. Same security boundary as venues.json: a path absent from this file is refused. Paths are static and were chosen by measuring price impact on chain - direct USDC pools for cbETH (-15.5% at $1k) and wstETH (-78.4% at $1k) are effectively dead, so those route through WETH. Fees are hundredths of a bip: 500 = 0.05%. Exits are the same hops reversed, quoted live with QuoterV2 at $1,000: WETH -0.0018%, cbBTC +0.0025%, wstETH -0.0034%, cbETH -0.0073%, USDbC -0.0012%, USDS -0.0085%, GHO -0.0055%, rETH -0.0113%, EURC -0.0289%, AERO -0.0329%, weETH -0.0506%. A hold venue you can enter and cannot leave is worse than no venue, so every entry path has its exit. tBTC is deliberately absent: its only v3 pools (cbBTC/tBTC at 100 and 500) hold about $100 and quote -14.7% at $100 and -91% at $1,000, so it stays unreachable rather than reachable at a loss. Nine further assets were re-measured against Chainlink at $100 and $1,000 in both directions; five cleared and are listed here. Entries at $1,000: DAI -0.050% (direct/100), USDT +0.030% (direct/100), USDe -0.028% (direct/500), WBTC -0.108% (USDC-500-cbBTC-100), VIRTUAL -0.477% (USDC-500-WETH-500). Exits at $1,000: DAI -0.019%, USDT -0.050%, USDe -0.073%, WBTC -0.017%, VIRTUAL +0.018%. Four failed the 0.5% bound on the EXIT leg on every v3 route tried, so they stay unreachable rather than reachable one-way: AAVE -0.644% (best exit, WETH500/3000), MORPHO -0.634% (WETH500/3000), VVV -0.690% (direct/3000), LINK -0.886% (direct/3000). Their entries all quoted better than -0.4%, which is why a buy-only pass looked like they cleared. Also measured and refused: tBTC -85%, LBTC -99.9%, ezETH -47.7%, AERO -0.539% on v3 (its depth is on Aerodrome), sUSDS -100%, cbXRP/DEGEN/COMP/WELL/MOG all worse than -1%.",
